WEBVTT

00:00:01.070 --> 00:00:05.520
<i>Heading into the second semester, 
we began work on our next project.</i>

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:09.030
<i>The script, storyboard, and location 
scouting all went smoothly,</i>

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:12.360
<i>which left us with just the matter 
of actually filming things. And then...</i>

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:13.570
You just don't get it!

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:14.980
You don't understand at all!

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:16.990
There can't be any dialog here!

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:19.360
A collision of different opinions!

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:19.790
You've got it backwards! 
There absolutely needs to be dialog here!

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:20.890
Now that's youth for you!

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:21.910
You don't even understand what I'm saying!

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:24.760
We need to start filming, 
so I should probably step in.

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:28.880
Hey, Shinoaki! You're gonna need to wake up.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:42.480
We starting now?

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:45.010
Y-Yeah, we should.

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:48.110
It's about time to get ready.

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:53.760
Nanako, we're gonna start 
shoo...ting... soon...

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:57.780
You ready? Lines all memorized?

00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:59.160
I've got it!

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.910
It's all up here, so I'm ready when you are!

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:04.290
That's great. I can tell you're motivated.

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:07.730
Well, yeah! I'm trying 
to become an actress.

00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:09.690
What's up with you, Kyoya?

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:11.410
I-It's nothing.

00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:13.260
I'm gonna check on Tsurayuki and Kawasegawa.

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:15.840
Have you two figured things out yet?

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:17.340
Kyoya, listen to this!

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:20.100
After we finally agreed 
to the cuts to the script,

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.480
now she's talking about how 
there might be more in the edit!

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:23.550
Obviously!

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:26.370
Filming is about collecting material! 
The final product is made in editing,

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:28.100
and sometimes you make 
judgment calls in that process!

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:31.300
Even if that's the case, do you really need 
to throw it in my face like an insult?!

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:34.080
If I don't say something now, 
you're just gonna complain later!

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:35.360
Look, we're running on limited time here.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:37.090
Let's try and film what we can now, okay?

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:41.800
I guess so. I really shouldn't be 
wasting my time arguing with <i>him.</i>

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:43.950
Whoa, hold up, I'm not through—

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:31.600
This doesn't sit right.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.440
Are you still mad about 
your wardrobe malfunction?

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:35.070
Not that!

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:39.510
I was talking about our 
equipment for the shoot.

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:40.820
The equipment?

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:45.660
First-year students aren't allowed 
to requisition equipment for multiple days.

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:49.830
But our shoot was scheduled 
for three days and two nights.

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:52.510
You did something, didn't you?

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:56.950
I actually need your help 
with something related to that.

00:03:58.460 --> 00:03:59.960
<b>O
o
n
a
k
a
 
A
r
t
 
S
c
h
o
o
l</b>

00:03:58.460 --> 00:03:59.960
<b>No Crossing</b>

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:00.650
I am so sorry!

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:03.020
We're actually filming up ahead,

00:04:03.020 --> 00:04:05.260
so could you wait for a moment, please?

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:07.480
Sure thing.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:09.930
We've got a pedestrian 
coming through. Is he clear?

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:12.120
<i>All clear.</i>

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:15.350
Sorry about the wait. Go right on through.

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:16.690
Much obliged.

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:19.590
Thank you for your cooperation!

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:21.260
I knew you'd be a huge help, Kawasegawa—

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:22.990
I wish you hadn't!

00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:27.660
Third-years are able to borrow 
equipment for a week at most.

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:31.830
So you volunteered to help some of them 
in exchange for access to their gear

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:34.870
on days when they wouldn't be using it.

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:36.710
It is technically against the rules, yeah.

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:38.880
Exactly! If our professor finds out—

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:41.920
Yeah, she's gonna be real pissed.

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:45.590
A... kid?

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:48.190
Where did you come from, little girl?

00:04:48.190 --> 00:04:52.230
You really wanna cop 
that attitude with a senpai, kid?

00:04:52.230 --> 00:04:53.790
S-Senpai?

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:57.490
See, I had heard there were some first-years

00:04:57.490 --> 00:05:00.350
willing to bust their humps for no reward,

00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:03.840
but that's the real deal? 
Makes sense, I guess.

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:05.740
Um... would you be willing 
to keep quiet about it?

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:07.070
You owe me.

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:11.220
The name's Tomioka Keiko.

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:14.360
I'll keep this under my hat, 
but I'm gonna collect some day.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:16.550
See ya around!

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:20.210
<b>Oonaka University of the Arts</b>

00:05:22.570 --> 00:05:25.720
<i>That was the film by Team Kitayama Plus.</i>

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:27.830
You did real good, Nanako!

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:31.750
Thanks! But I still feel kinda 
embarrassed about it.

00:05:32.340 --> 00:05:34.230
They seemed to like it, Kawasegawa.

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:36.260
Something's off.

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:40.720
It never quite got past feeling scripted.

00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:43.980
It was put together well enough, 
but that was all.

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:45.940
There was nothing to elevate it.

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:47.480
I'm sure you're overthinking it.

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:51.690
It came together really well, 
and people seemed to like it.

00:05:52.850 --> 00:05:54.500
I hope you're right.

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:58.500
<i>This will be the final film 
of the screening.</i>

00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:15.350
<i>What is this?</i>

00:06:15.790 --> 00:06:19.900
<i>It's totally different. The acting 
is on a completely different level.</i>

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:26.980
That last one was good, too, 
but the acting here is way better.

00:06:26.980 --> 00:06:29.740
Seriously. It makes the other one 
seem like a school play.

00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:32.910
The last team's acting 
held the whole thing back.

00:06:35.670 --> 00:06:38.210
And the first place film this time...

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:40.620
was produced by Team Kitayama Plus.

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:43.380
You did a good job. Congratulations.

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:45.430
Wait, they won?

00:06:45.430 --> 00:06:47.570
In terms of acting, it was
 like a 10-to-1 disadvantage...

00:06:47.570 --> 00:06:49.860
That concludes class for today.

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:51.740
Professor!

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:55.140
Wasn't the ranking kind of weird back there?

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:56.220
What do you mean?

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:58.740
I mean, the last film was clearly just...

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:01.300
The acting was so much better! 
Enough to blow everything else—

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:03.660
Visual media is a comprehensive art form.

00:07:04.330 --> 00:07:06.790
Even if one actor's performance 
is particularly well done,

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:10.330
that doesn't automatically 
add points for other areas.

00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:11.410
B-But...

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:16.140
In that case, can you tell me 
the fundamental reason

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:18.870
that film had such a strong impact, Kogure?

00:07:19.930 --> 00:07:24.030
Technical acting ability. Experience. 
Appearance. Voice quality.

00:07:24.030 --> 00:07:26.840
Acting is the result of a lot 
of different factors.

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:30.580
But there was a more simple 
deciding factor this time around.

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:32.890
They were serious.

00:07:34.670 --> 00:07:35.890
That's all.

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:45.360
Karaoke

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:45.360
Good work, everyone!

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:49.700
Thanks to all of you, we were 
able to put together a great film.

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:52.580
All right, here we go! Cheers!

00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:54.070
Cheers!

00:07:54.070 --> 00:07:56.430
Filming at the beach sure was hot, huh?

00:07:56.430 --> 00:07:59.100
Yeah! But the project came together great!

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:02.170
I'd say that scene was all about 
the quality of my script!

00:08:02.170 --> 00:08:05.220
Even though your lines kept getting cut?

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:06.600
You sure about that?

00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:07.590
Shut up!

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:12.520
I didn't expect first place, though!

00:08:11.560 --> 00:08:13.840
Is she going to be okay?

00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:16.690
I mean, how was a team 
with me on it gonna do that well?

00:08:14.530 --> 00:08:16.690
She's pretty clearly faking her cheer.

00:08:17.170 --> 00:08:20.520
It looks to me like she's trying 
to avoid dealing with something.

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:21.180
Tell me about it!

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:22.730
I think she just needs some space.

00:08:22.730 --> 00:08:25.420
It should clear up with time.

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:27.860
Time, huh?

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:30.030
Okay, Nanako, you're up!

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:32.490
I-I shouldn't...

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:34.720
Yeah, you should! Just belt one out!

00:08:34.720 --> 00:08:36.480
You'll feel great!

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:38.830
Should I, Kyoya?

00:08:39.190 --> 00:08:40.120
Why not?

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:43.740
They were bound to hear it 
at some point, anyway.

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:45.120
It's just a question of when.

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:54.050
I guess you're right. Okay...

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:59.620
Karaoke

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:12.980
Sorry about how terrible that was!

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:17.240
Nanako, your voice really rings out!

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:19.540
Hell, yeah! It carries even better than mine!

00:09:19.540 --> 00:09:23.040
It's probably because of that minyo folk 
singing you did when you were little, right?

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:24.920
That was pretty impressive!

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:27.250
I guess so...

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:29.710
So, who wants to go next?

00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:31.840
Kawasegawa?

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:34.130
You gonna sing next?

00:09:35.250 --> 00:09:38.050
You weren't serious 
about being an actor, then.

00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:41.390
You want this, don't you? To be a singer.

00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:45.640
Why would you say that?

00:09:45.640 --> 00:09:48.140
Because I thought it was strange.

00:09:48.140 --> 00:09:50.320
It's true that you could perform in bits,

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:54.160
but there was no feeling 
of intentionality behind it.

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:56.780
It always felt superficial.

00:09:57.080 --> 00:10:01.190
That makes sense. And explains why it 
never stopped feeling artificial, too.

00:10:01.190 --> 00:10:02.710
It's not like that!

00:10:02.710 --> 00:10:04.490
It actually is.

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:07.960
Because you weren't serious about acting.

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:12.040
You can claim otherwise, 
but the proof is in the performance.

00:10:12.890 --> 00:10:15.320
If you can project your voice so well,

00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:18.110
it must mean you've been practicing in one 
way or another since you were little, right?

00:10:18.550 --> 00:10:23.170
So why would you try to act, 
instead of following your passion?

00:10:23.170 --> 00:10:24.510
Shut up.

00:10:24.840 --> 00:10:27.360
It's because you're scared 
of taking it seriously, right?

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:30.400
Because if you start taking something you've 
always cared about seriously, and fail?

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:33.100
It would refute everything you stand for.

00:10:33.100 --> 00:10:35.190
You were afraid of committing.

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:37.610
So instead, because you got 
compliments before, you turned to acting,

00:10:37.610 --> 00:10:39.580
and lied about wanting to be an actress.

00:10:39.580 --> 00:10:41.620
Shut up! Just stop talking!

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:43.740
What do you know?!

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:47.320
I've loved singing, grown up around music,

00:10:47.320 --> 00:10:49.550
but have always been tone deaf.

00:10:49.550 --> 00:10:53.910
If I could do something about it, 
I would have by now!

00:10:54.860 --> 00:10:56.540
But you haven't.

00:10:57.670 --> 00:11:00.520
Then why did you join 
the visual arts program?

00:11:00.520 --> 00:11:02.820
You should've gone straight for music.

00:11:02.820 --> 00:11:04.540
You might not've been 
able to fix it at home,

00:11:04.540 --> 00:11:07.220
but things could be different 
at a proper school.

00:11:07.610 --> 00:11:11.010
So why did you give up 
at the most crucial moment?

00:11:11.010 --> 00:11:12.460
Because...

00:11:13.700 --> 00:11:15.780
Nanako's been practicing, though.

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:17.850
We come here all the time—

00:11:17.850 --> 00:11:19.800
But has she taken actual singing lessons?

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:22.110
And do you have the right 
knowledge to help her?

00:11:22.680 --> 00:11:23.410
Well...

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:25.520
I don't think that counts as practice.

00:11:25.520 --> 00:11:28.160
She's just been pretending 
to put in some effort.

00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:32.830
What a waste of a gift.

00:11:34.580 --> 00:11:36.460
Stop running away, and get serious!

00:11:37.340 --> 00:11:39.350
If you have something you 
can seriously chase after,

00:11:39.350 --> 00:11:42.160
why wouldn't you make it 
your weapon of choice?!

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:45.520
Instead you flit off to acting because 
someone gave you some casual compliments!

00:11:45.520 --> 00:11:47.560
That won't ever move anyone!

00:11:48.890 --> 00:11:49.600
Nanako!

00:11:52.890 --> 00:11:54.190
You can hit me.

00:11:54.950 --> 00:11:57.680
I realize what I've said deserves it.

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:00.800
I'm going.

00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:01.540
Nanako!

00:12:01.540 --> 00:12:02.570
Don't follow me!

00:12:08.130 --> 00:12:09.450
I should go, too.

00:12:09.980 --> 00:12:11.370
Kawasegawa...

00:12:11.370 --> 00:12:14.760
If Nanako wants, I'll quit the team.

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:16.960
I'm sorry for causing so much trouble.

00:12:29.320 --> 00:12:30.310
Nanako!

00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:33.740
Sorry. I don't feel like talking right now.

00:12:35.060 --> 00:12:36.420
It didn't work, huh?

00:12:36.420 --> 00:12:38.710
It felt like I had no ground to stand on.

00:12:38.710 --> 00:12:43.360
Damn it! Queen Kawasegawa had to go 
and make a mess of things.

00:12:43.660 --> 00:12:49.330
I think I want Nanako to sing, too, though.

00:12:49.780 --> 00:12:51.120
Shinoaki...

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:53.970
I mean, that's what she 
really cares about, right?

00:12:53.970 --> 00:12:57.740
That's the only reason what 
Kawasegawa-san said hit her so hard.

00:12:57.740 --> 00:13:00.890
Well, she was going to have to deal 
with it sooner or later.

00:13:00.890 --> 00:13:05.220
Better for her to wrestle with it now 
instead of looking back when it's too late.

00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:06.990
I guess...

00:13:07.480 --> 00:13:09.550
She should figure out what 
she really wants, try it,

00:13:09.550 --> 00:13:13.100
and if it doesn't work out... the sooner 
she can hang it up, the better.

00:13:16.720 --> 00:13:19.320
Anyway, I gotta get to work...

00:13:19.320 --> 00:13:21.020
Are you okay? You seem tired.

00:13:21.020 --> 00:13:24.070
I've had back-to-back shifts lately.

00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:26.270
I'm gonna get plenty of sleep 
when I come home.

00:13:26.270 --> 00:13:27.530
You be careful, now.

00:13:27.770 --> 00:13:28.740
Right.

00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:33.890
What did you want to talk about?

00:13:35.060 --> 00:13:38.210
If this is about quitting 
the team, I don't accept.

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:42.650
I genuinely feel bad 
about what I said to Nanako.

00:13:42.650 --> 00:13:44.650
And I've made trouble 
for you as a result.

00:13:44.650 --> 00:13:46.950
It's been no trouble for me,

00:13:46.950 --> 00:13:49.970
and I think you said something 
that Nanako needed to hear.

00:13:50.440 --> 00:13:53.350
But she's still depressed, isn't she?

00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:55.580
It's her problem to work through.

00:13:55.580 --> 00:13:57.870
You shouldn't take it personally, Kawasegawa.

00:14:00.120 --> 00:14:01.980
I was jealous of her.

00:14:02.530 --> 00:14:04.360
Jealous of Nanako?

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:05.680
That's right.

00:14:06.170 --> 00:14:08.380
She has a talent that really shines,

00:14:08.380 --> 00:14:11.210
and has been working on it 
ever since she was little.

00:14:11.210 --> 00:14:14.540
But she was pretending to not care 
about it, so I got angry.

00:14:15.490 --> 00:14:19.580
She's got such an expressive voice, 
one that can enchant so many people.

00:14:19.580 --> 00:14:21.610
She's cute and glamorous.

00:14:21.610 --> 00:14:25.000
It really made me realize that girls like her 
are the ones that become stars.

00:14:27.400 --> 00:14:29.440
Which is why I'm worried...

00:14:29.440 --> 00:14:30.880
It'll be okay.

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:35.620
Nanako isn't going to let this stop her. 
I'll figure something out.

00:14:35.620 --> 00:14:37.530
Do you have an idea?

00:14:37.530 --> 00:14:42.610
Not yet. But I know how 
passionate she is about singing.

00:14:42.610 --> 00:14:46.150
If I can just remind her of that, 
I think she'll be set.

00:14:46.630 --> 00:14:49.590
It's weird. There's no real basis 
to what you just said,

00:14:49.590 --> 00:14:52.410
but something about it 
makes me want to believe you.

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:56.120
Y-You think?

00:14:57.160 --> 00:14:59.010
Oh, hello there.

00:14:59.010 --> 00:14:59.850
Are you headed to class?

00:14:59.850 --> 00:15:02.430
Nah, we've got preparations 
for the school festival's concert.

00:15:02.430 --> 00:15:04.720
We're on the production committee.

00:15:04.720 --> 00:15:06.240
Sorry, we need to hurry!

00:15:06.240 --> 00:15:07.420
The school festival...

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:10.180
What do you mean, you don't know 
about the school festival?!

00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:13.810
W-Well, that's why I was asking...

00:15:13.810 --> 00:15:15.310
Allow me to enlighten you!

00:15:15.310 --> 00:15:16.980
Since the school's founding 40 years ago,

00:15:15.390 --> 00:15:19.770
<b>Entrance</b>

00:15:16.980 --> 00:15:19.780
nearly its entire 8,000-strong 
student body has participated

00:15:19.780 --> 00:15:22.560
in a massive annual celebration 
that lasts over three days,

00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:26.310
with visitor numbers estimated
 in the tens of thousands!

00:15:26.310 --> 00:15:28.740
That's the Oonaka Arts School Festival!

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:30.670
O-Okay.

00:15:30.710 --> 00:15:33.920
And naturally, the Fine Arts Club 
will be participating, too!

00:15:33.920 --> 00:15:37.120
And yet in the face of such an
 honored tradition, you seem to have no idea—

00:15:38.960 --> 00:15:42.880
Where do you get off lecturing people after 
what you used that honored tradition for?!

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:44.550
I'm sorry.

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:48.000
<b>I am not allowed to talk</b>

00:15:49.060 --> 00:15:52.220
Uh... what happened, exactly?

00:15:52.220 --> 00:15:57.050
Our club has always taken a classroom, 
and run an art exhibition there.

00:15:57.050 --> 00:15:58.520
Are you doing it again this year—

00:15:58.520 --> 00:15:59.850
That <i>was</i> the plan!

00:16:00.620 --> 00:16:03.650
But this idiot submitted 
a crazy idea instead!

00:16:03.650 --> 00:16:06.590
What did you ask to do?

00:16:06.590 --> 00:16:07.830
A maid café.

00:16:07.830 --> 00:16:08.520
What?

00:16:08.520 --> 00:16:10.530
I've always dreamed of it, you know?!

00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:13.070
Having cute girls dressed up like maids.

00:16:13.070 --> 00:16:16.070
And then getting pictures of us 
having a fun conversation—

00:16:16.070 --> 00:16:18.010
You're not allowed to talk!

00:16:18.010 --> 00:16:19.550
R-Right...

00:16:20.930 --> 00:16:22.700
We're past the deadline for changing plans,

00:16:22.700 --> 00:16:24.940
so now I have to figure out how 
to recruit enough people.

00:16:24.940 --> 00:16:27.250
I want our star girl to have pink hair!

00:16:28.150 --> 00:16:30.380
I feel like this is awakening 
something inside of me!

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:32.270
Where do you get off making demands?!

00:16:34.960 --> 00:16:37.490
There was something I wanted to ask you all.

00:16:38.760 --> 00:16:40.710
A tiny pink-haired—

00:16:40.970 --> 00:16:42.470
Pink hair, huh?

00:16:42.470 --> 00:16:45.900
We've got plenty of students 
like that, though.

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:47.150
I see...

00:16:47.150 --> 00:16:50.310
Oh, I think she said her name was Tomioka.

00:16:50.310 --> 00:16:51.420
Keiko, right.

00:16:51.420 --> 00:16:54.690
Right! And she had a Kansai 
accent, just like that...

00:16:56.610 --> 00:16:57.460
Yo.

00:16:58.280 --> 00:17:01.130
Tomioka...senpai?!

00:17:01.130 --> 00:17:02.370
Just call me Keiko.

00:17:02.370 --> 00:17:05.980
Hashy! Who is this pink-haired little darling?!

00:17:05.980 --> 00:17:07.700
Upsy-daisy...

00:17:08.160 --> 00:17:10.630
Man, I ain't been by the art club in a bit.

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:12.660
Does Hiroe-chan still come around?

00:17:12.660 --> 00:17:15.130
Huh? Hiroe-senpai, you mean?

00:17:15.130 --> 00:17:17.430
She graduated two years ago.

00:17:17.670 --> 00:17:19.360
Seriously?

00:17:19.360 --> 00:17:22.230
The kid's finally graduated, huh?

00:17:22.230 --> 00:17:25.190
Excuse me, but did you need something?

00:17:25.190 --> 00:17:26.940
Oh, right, now that you mention it...

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:29.310
Almost forgot what I came here for.

00:17:29.660 --> 00:17:32.020
I figured it was time you paid me back.

00:17:32.540 --> 00:17:35.070
You wanna come work on our game?

00:17:36.220 --> 00:17:36.950
A game?

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:40.910
Hallucigenia Soft?! They're one 
of the big name dojin circles!

00:17:40.910 --> 00:17:44.450
Yep. And I was wondering if you'd wanna 
come on and direct something for us.

00:17:44.450 --> 00:17:46.540
Why me?

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:48.970
I asked some of the kids 
working on the shoot,

00:17:48.970 --> 00:17:52.470
and they said you've got some slick moves 
in the production department.

00:17:52.470 --> 00:17:54.570
I don't know about that...

00:17:54.570 --> 00:17:56.310
Quit trying to be modest!

00:17:56.310 --> 00:17:58.650
So how about it? Wanna give a shot?

00:17:59.120 --> 00:18:02.890
<i>I could work on games again... 
give my dream another shot.</i>

00:18:02.890 --> 00:18:03.970
<i>But...</i>

00:18:03.970 --> 00:18:04.970
I'm sorry!

00:18:05.480 --> 00:18:07.980
I can't... not right now.

00:18:11.490 --> 00:18:13.270
Seems you've got a full plate, huh?

00:18:14.950 --> 00:18:15.900
I'm sorry.

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:19.020
Hey, the offer's still on the table, all right?

00:18:19.020 --> 00:18:20.820
You still owe me one, after all.

00:18:21.290 --> 00:18:22.960
I appreciate it.

00:18:22.960 --> 00:18:24.830
Since I'm here, you can have these.

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:27.830
<b>Chasing The Morning Sun</b>

00:18:25.400 --> 00:18:27.830
They should give you an idea what we're doing.

00:18:28.170 --> 00:18:29.460
Catch ya next time.

00:18:30.210 --> 00:18:32.210
<i>Right now, I don't have what it takes.</i>

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:30.710
Tomioka Keiko

00:18:30.710 --> 00:18:30.830
Tomioka Keiko

00:18:30.830 --> 00:18:30.960
Tomioka Keiko

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:32.210
Tomioka Keiko

00:18:33.030 --> 00:18:35.710
<i>Not to go after what I want seriously.</i>

00:18:40.640 --> 00:18:41.720
<i>Amazing.</i>

00:18:42.550 --> 00:18:45.070
<i>Their quality is on par 
with commercial companies.</i>

00:18:45.070 --> 00:18:47.500
<i>They actually got CONOCO-san to record this.</i>

00:18:47.500 --> 00:18:50.020
<i>We never had that kind of budget.</i>

00:18:51.150 --> 00:18:53.850
<i>And the singer that we did hire for our game</i>

00:18:53.850 --> 00:18:57.280
<i>had to be adjusted a lot 
in the mix to be presentable.</i>

00:18:57.740 --> 00:19:00.170
<i>And since we didn't have 
the money to hire someone,</i>

00:19:00.170 --> 00:19:02.060
<i>I ended up having to do it.</i>

00:19:02.060 --> 00:19:05.440
<i>I still remember spending the night 
at the office for that.</i>

00:19:07.470 --> 00:19:09.430
<i>Wait, this might just be it!</i>

00:19:12.030 --> 00:19:14.130
Nanako... Nanako?

00:19:14.930 --> 00:19:18.870
I said I didn't feel like talking. Sorry.

00:19:18.870 --> 00:19:20.740
I just need a minute, please.

00:19:20.740 --> 00:19:21.630
No!

00:19:22.160 --> 00:19:25.120
I don't have anything right now.

00:19:25.120 --> 00:19:28.910
It's all been smashed completely... 
and there's nothing left.

00:19:29.350 --> 00:19:33.490
I have nothing to say to anyone... 
so I don't want to talk.

00:19:33.490 --> 00:19:36.320
I know. But you do still have something.

00:19:37.030 --> 00:19:40.070
Something that is very important, Nanako.

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:44.570
So I'm not leaving until you hear me out.

00:19:45.320 --> 00:19:48.300
<i>I brushed against 
the freckles that I hated so...</i>

00:19:48.300 --> 00:19:51.160
<i>Life goes on and I heave 
a little sigh for you.</i>

00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:53.780
<i>It's heavy, the love 
that I once shared with you...</i>

00:19:53.780 --> 00:19:56.590
<i>But it dissolved like 
it was just a sugar cube.</i>

00:19:56.590 --> 00:19:59.520
<i>Now the little pain sitting in my heart...</i>

00:19:59.520 --> 00:20:02.670
<i>Has shrunken a bit, 
but it really does hurt me now.</i>

00:20:00.660 --> 00:20:04.640
Is this... my voice?

00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:08.760
That's right. It's what your singing 
can ultimately sound like.

00:20:08.760 --> 00:20:10.980
All I did was adjust it.

00:20:11.500 --> 00:20:12.780
Adjust?

00:20:12.780 --> 00:20:17.810
Yeah. I adjusted the tone just 
a little bit. Nothing else.

00:20:17.810 --> 00:20:20.610
Which is why I can say for sure 
that this is your singing.

00:20:21.850 --> 00:20:24.110
I needed you to hear it.

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:27.120
Your singing has incredible potential!

00:20:27.650 --> 00:20:29.340
And I wanted you to know.

00:20:43.550 --> 00:20:46.640
S-Sorry! Should I have not brought it up?

00:20:46.640 --> 00:20:48.670
Thank you, Kyoya.

00:20:49.510 --> 00:20:55.290
I... I've been singing for so long, 
but I never liked the way it sounded.

00:20:55.290 --> 00:20:59.170
I could never get the right pitch, 
and it wouldn't sound like I wanted it to.

00:20:59.520 --> 00:21:05.320
So I thought I could try acting, 
where I could at least use my voice.

00:21:05.320 --> 00:21:08.350
But that wasn't the right way, was it?

00:21:08.350 --> 00:21:12.330
I think now I understand what Kawasegawa 
and the professor were saying.

00:21:12.740 --> 00:21:15.960
I can't hope to beat people 
who are really taking it seriously.

00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:18.840
And there's no way my 
acting can move people.

00:21:20.200 --> 00:21:22.560
I want to get better at singing.

00:21:22.560 --> 00:21:25.100
I'll study for real, practice for real,

00:21:25.100 --> 00:21:27.490
and let people hear what 
I can do when I'm serious.

00:21:27.810 --> 00:21:32.100
I want to sing a lot of amazing songs, 
and touch people's hearts.

00:21:32.890 --> 00:21:37.310
Do you think I'll be able to do it? 
Will I be able to go that far?

00:21:37.310 --> 00:21:39.110
I'm sure you can.

00:21:39.580 --> 00:21:43.100
I have an idea! Will you try it 
with me, Nanako?

00:21:43.720 --> 00:21:44.820
Oh, sorry!

00:21:47.280 --> 00:21:50.050
I'm going to trust you, Kyoya!

00:21:50.050 --> 00:21:53.950
So help me figure out singing! Please?

00:21:54.250 --> 00:21:56.510
You're going to be doing all the work.

00:21:56.510 --> 00:22:01.100
But I'll do whatever I can to help you.

00:22:01.100 --> 00:22:04.960
Yeah! I'm going to figure 
something out, damn it!
